## 5. Windows Firewall Configuration

As part of the controlled lab scenario, Windows Defender Firewall was intentionally disabled.

The firewall was turned off for:

* Domain networks
* Private networks
* Public networks

### Visual Representation

![Windows Defender Firewall Disabled](images/firewall-disabled.png)

*Windows Defender Firewall intentionally disabled as part of the weakened-defense scenario.*

The Windows system displayed warnings showing that the firewall was no longer using the recommended settings.

### Defensive Meaning

Disabling the firewall did not automatically create a DoS condition, but it intentionally removed an important security layer.

With the firewall enabled, inbound traffic is evaluated against configured rules before being allowed to reach exposed services.

Removing that protection can:

* Increase the exposed attack surface
* Allow more unwanted network traffic
* Reduce host-level filtering
* Make services easier to reach directly

This part of the lab demonstrated how a weakened security configuration can increase the impact of network attacks.

